    "description": "<p>CONTEXT</p><p>Person Account uniqueness for Players and Referrers is enforced by Account.Email_Record_Type_Unique__c (Text 255, unique index), stamped by the flow &quot;Account - Before Save - Set Unique Email Address for Person Accounts&quot; as:</p><p>RecordType.DeveloperName + &quot;:&quot; + LOWER(TRIM(PersonEmail))</p><p>This is what allows a Player and a Referrer to legitimately share an email address (different keys) while blocking two Players on the same address — including the async race where a batch of Study Link Clicks for the same person creates duplicate Players.</p><p>If PersonEmail is blank, no key is stamp185ed and the record sits outside the duplicate guard entirely.</p><p>The SLC flow already blocks blank emails on the integration path (Has Email decision before the email match, sets Processing Status = Review Required with reason &quot;Blank Email Address&quot;). This ticket closes the manual UI path.</p><p>ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA</p><p>1. Saving a Player or Referrer Person Account with a blank PersonEmail is blocked, on both create and edit.</p><p>2. Operator and Partner (business) Accounts are unaffected.</p><p>3. Error displays on the PersonEmail field.</p><p>IMPLEMENTATION</p><p>Rule name: Player_Referrer_PersonEmail_Required</p><p>Formula:</p><p>AND(</p><p>OR(</p><p>RecordType.DeveloperName = &quot;Player&quot;,</p><p>RecordType.DeveloperName = &quot;Referrer&quot;</p><p>),</p><p>ISBLANK(PersonEmail)</p><p>)</p><p>Error message: Email is required for Player and Referrer records.</p><p>Error location: PersonEmail field</p><p>TEST NOTES</p><p>Create Player with blank email -&gt; blocked</p><p>Create Referrer with blank email -&gt; blocked</p><p>Create Operator / Partner with no email -&gt; allowed</p><p>Edit existing Player, clear email -&gt; blocked</p><p>Reprocess an SLC with a valid email -&gt; still completes normally</p><p>DEPLOY NOTE</p><p>Assumes zero existing Player/Referrer records with a blank PersonEmail (confirmed by Kobi 2026-08-27). Re-confirm with a count in the target org before promoting past Partial SB — if any exist, every subsequent save on those records will fail. If legacy blanks turn up, add a grandfathering clause:</p><p>OR(ISNEW(), NOT(ISBLANK(PRIORVALUE(PersonEmail))))</p><p>Validation rules also apply to Flow DML, so this doubles as a backstop if a blank ever slips past the SLC guard.</p><p>RELATED</p><p>BUILD-194 — Referrer: Dedup-on-Create (hard block)</p><p>BUILD-230 — Player: Manage Duplicate Player</p><p>BUILD-03 — Player/Referrer matching, duplicate prevention, and cross-linking</p><p>Created 2026-08-27 from the SLC duplicate-Player race review.</p>",
